+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_LyxWioD8pi5yGOl2Rits0583","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /workspace/CONTRACT.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e285a961-1a48-49d1-9407-6a92b42829e5","uuid":"c06247d9-dfd1-410c-95ec-72b705a1c028","timestamp":"2026-05-31T04:27:18.464Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/workspace/CONTRACT.md","content":"# DocumentStore Contract\n\n## 1. Document CRUD\n\n### 1.1 Create\n- **Behavior**: `create(id, content)` stores a new document on the current branch.\n- **Verified**: `create(\"doc1\", {a: 1})` succeeds. `get(\"doc1\")` returns `{a: 1}`.\n\n### 1.2 Create throws on duplicate\n- **Behavior**: `create(id, content)` throws if the ID already exists (and is not deleted) on the current branch.\n- **Verified**: `create(\"doc1\", {a: 1}); create(\"doc1\", {a: 2})` throws an error with message containing \"already exists\".\n\n### 1.3 Create works after delete (re-create)\n- **Behavior**: After deleting a document, `create` with the same ID works (it's no longer considered existing).\n- **Verified**: `create(\"doc1\", {a:1}); delete(\"doc1\"); create(\"doc1\", {b:2})` succeeds. `get(\"doc1\")` returns `{b:2}`.\n\n### 1.4 Get returns deep clone\n- **Behavior**: `get(id)` returns a deep clone — mutations to the returned object don't affect the store.\n- **Verified**: After `create(\"doc1\", {a: {b: 1}})`, `const o = get(\"doc1\"); o.a.b = 99; get(\"doc1\").a.b` is still `1`.\n\n### 1.5 Get throws if not found\n- **Behavior**: `get(id)` throws if the document doesn't exist on the current branch.\n- **Verified**: `get(\"nonexistent\")` throws with message containing \"not found\".\n\n### 1.6 Get throws if deleted\n- **Behavior**: `get(id)` throws if the document has been deleted on the current branch.\n- **Verified**: `create(\"doc1\", {a:1}); delete(\"doc1\"); get(\"doc1\")` throws with message containing \"not found\".\n\n### 1.7 Update changes content\n- **Behavior**: `update(id, content)` replaces the document content.\n- **Verified**: `create(\"doc1\", {a:1}); update(\"doc1\", {b:2}); get(\"doc1\")` returns `{b:2}`.\n\n### 1.8 Update throws if not found\n- **Behavior**: `update(id, content)` throws if the document doesn't exist.\n- **Verified**: `update(\"nonexistent\", {a:1})` throws with message containing \"not found\".\n\n### 1.9 Update throws if deleted\n- **Behavior**: `update(id, content)` throws if the document has been deleted.\n- **Verified**: `create(\"doc1\", {a:1}); delete(\"doc1\"); update(\"doc1\", {b:2})` throws with message containing \"not found\".\n\n### 1.10 Delete removes document\n- **Behavior**: `delete(id)` marks a document as deleted on the current branch.\n- **Verified**: `create(\"doc1\", {a:1}); delete(\"doc1\"); get(\"doc1\")` throws.\n\n### 1.11 Delete throws if not found\n- **Behavior**: `delete(id)` throws if the document doesn't exist.\n- **Verified**: `delete(\"nonexistent\")` throws with message containing \"not found\".\n\n### 1.12 Delete throws if already deleted\n- **Behavior**: `delete(id)` throws if already deleted.\n- **Verified**: `create(\"doc1\", {a:1}); delete(\"doc1\"); delete(\"doc1\")` throws.\n\n### 1.13 Create stores deep clone\n- **Behavior**: `create(id, content)` stores a deep clone — mutations to the original object don't affect the store.\n- **Verified**: `const obj = {a: {b: 1}}; create(\"doc1\", obj); obj.a.b = 99; get(\"doc1\").a.b` is still `1`.\n\n### 1.14 Update stores deep clone\n- **Behavior**: `update(id, content)` stores a deep clone.\n- **Verified**: `create(\"doc1\", {a:1}); const obj = {b: {c: 2}}; update(\"doc1\", obj); obj.b.c = 99; get(\"doc1\").b.c` is still `2`.\n\n## 2. Version History\n\n### 2.1 Create generates a version\n- **Behavior**: `create(id, content)` creates the first version.\n- **Verified**: After `create(\"doc1\", {a:1})`, `getHistory(\"doc1\")` returns an array with 1 entry. `version.content` equals `{a:1}`.\n\n### 2.2 Update generates versions\n- **Behavior**: Each `update(id, content)` creates a new version.\n- **Verified**: `create(\"doc1\", {a:1}); update(\"doc1\", {b:2}); getHistory(\"doc1\")` has 2 entries.\n\n### 2.3 Delete does NOT generate a version\n- **Behavior**: `delete(id)` does not create a version.\n- **Verified**: `create(\"doc1\", {a:1}); delete(\"doc1\"); getHistory(\"doc1\")` still has 1 entry (from create).\n\n### 2.4 History is chronological (oldest first)\n- **Behavior**: Versions are returned oldest first.\n- **Verified**: `create(\"doc1\", {v:1}); update(\"doc1\", {v:2}); update(\"doc1\", {v:3}); const h = getHistory(\"doc1\"); h[0].content.v === 1; h[1].content.v === 2; h[2].content.v === 3`.\n\n### 2.5 Version has id, timestamp, content\n- **Behavior**: Each Version has `id` (string), `timestamp` (number), `content` (object).\n- **Verified**: `const v = getHistory(\"doc1\")[0]; typeof v.id === \"string\"; typeof v.timestamp === \"number\"; typeof v.content === \"object\"`.\n\n### 2.6 Version IDs are unique\n- **Behavior**: No two versions have the same ID.\n- **Verified**: Create and update multiple documents. Collect all version IDs — no duplicates.\n\n### 2.7 getVersion returns specific version content\n- **Behavior**: `getVersion(id, versionId)` returns the content at that version (deep cloned).\n- **Verified**: `create(\"doc1\", {a:1}); const h = getHistory(\"doc1\"); getVersion(\"doc1\", h[0].id)` returns `{a:1}`.\n\n### 2.8 getVersion returns deep clone\n- **Behavior**: `getVersion` returns a deep clone.\n- **Verified**: `const v = getVersion(\"doc1\", vid); v.a = 99; getVersion(\"doc1\", vid).a` is still `1`.\n\n### 2.9 getVersion throws for bad version ID\n- **Behavior**: `getVersion(id, badVersionId)` throws if version not found.\n- **Verified**: `create(\"doc1\", {a:1}); getVersion(\"doc1\", \"nonexistent\")` throws.\n\n### 2.10 getVersion throws for bad document ID\n- **Behavior