+# DocumentStore Contract
+
+## 1. Document CRUD
+
+### 1.1 Create
+- **Behavior**: `create(id, content)` stores a new document on the current branch.
+- **Verified**: `create("doc1", {a: 1})` succeeds. `get("doc1")` returns `{a: 1}`.
+
+### 1.2 Create throws on duplicate
+- **Behavior**: `create(id, content)` throws if the ID already exists (and is not deleted) on the current branch.
+- **Verified**: `create("doc1", {a: 1}); create("doc1", {a: 2})` throws an error with message containing "already exists".
+
+### 1.3 Create works after delete (re-create)
+- **Behavior**: After deleting a document, `create` with the same ID works (it's no longer considered existing).
+- **Verified**: `create("doc1", {a:1}); delete("doc1"); create("doc1", {b:2})` succeeds. `get("doc1")` returns `{b:2}`.
+
+### 1.4 Get returns deep clone
+- **Behavior**: `get(id)` returns a deep clone — mutations to the returned object don't affect the store.
+- **Verified**: After `create("doc1", {a: {b: 1}})`, `const o = get("doc1"); o.a.b = 99; get("doc1").a.b` is still `1`.
+
+### 1.5 Get throws if not found
+- **Behavior**: `get(id)` throws if the document doesn't exist on the current branch.
+- **Verified**: `get("nonexistent")` throws with message containing "not found".
+
+### 1.6 Get throws if deleted
+- **Behavior**: `get(id)` throws if the document has been deleted on the current branch.
+- **Verified**: `create("doc1", {a:1}); delete("doc1"); get("doc1")` throws with message containing "not found".
+
+### 1.7 Update changes content
+- **Behavior**: `update(id, content)` replaces the document content.
+- **Verified**: `create("doc1", {a:1}); update("doc1", {b:2}); get("doc1")` returns `{b:2}`.
+
+### 1.8 Update throws if not found
+- **Behavior**: `update(id, content)` throws if the document doesn't exist.
+- **Verified**: `update("nonexistent", {a:1})` throws with message containing "not found".
+
+### 1.9 Update throws if deleted
+- **Behavior**: `update(id, content)` throws if the document has been deleted.
+- **Verified**: `create("doc1", {a:1}); delete("doc1"); update("doc1", {b:2})` throws with message containing "not found".
+
+### 1.10 Delete removes document
+- **Behavior**: `delete(id)` marks a document as deleted on the current branch.
+- **Verified**: `create("doc1", {a:1}); delete("doc1"); get("doc1")` throws.
+
+### 1.11 Delete throws if not found
+- **Behavior**: `delete(id)` throws if the document doesn't exist.
+- **Verified**: `delete("nonexistent")` throws with message containing "not found".
+
+### 1.12 Delete throws if already deleted
+- **Behavior**: `delete(id)` throws if already deleted.
+- **Verified**: `create("doc1", {a:1}); delete("doc1"); delete("doc1")` throws.
+
+### 1.13 Create stores deep clone
+- **Behavior**: `create(id, content)` stores a deep clone — mutations to the original object don't affect the store.
+- **Verified**: `const obj = {a: {b: 1}}; create("doc1", obj); obj.a.b = 99; get("doc1").a.b` is still `1`.
+
+### 1.14 Update stores deep clone
+- **Behavior**: `update(id, content)` stores a deep clone.
+- **Verified**: `create("doc1", {a:1}); const obj = {b: {c: 2}}; update("doc1", obj); obj.b.c = 99; get("doc1").b.c` is still `2`.
+
+## 2. Version History
+
+### 2.1 Create generates a version
+- **Behavior**: `create(id, content)` creates the first version.
+- **Verified**: After `create("doc1", {a:1})`, `getHistory("doc1")` returns an array with 1 entry. `version.content` equals `{a:1}`.
+
+### 2.2 Update generates versions
+- **Behavior**: Each `update(id, content)` creates a new version.
+- **Verified**: `create("doc1", {a:1}); update("doc1", {b:2}); getHistory("doc1")` has 2 entries.
+
+### 2.3 Delete does NOT generate a version
+- **Behavior**: `delete(id)` does not create a version.
+- **Verified**: `create("doc1", {a:1}); delete("doc1"); getHistory("doc1")` still has 1 entry (from create).
+
+### 2.4 History is chronological (oldest first)
+- **Behavior**: Versions are returned oldest first.
+- **Verified**: `create("doc1", {v:1}); update("doc1", {v:2}); update("doc1", {v:3}); const h = getHistory("doc1"); h[0].content.v === 1; h[1].content.v === 2; h[2].content.v === 3`.
+
+### 2.5 Version has id, timestamp, content
+- **Behavior**: Each Version has `id` (string), `timestamp` (number), `content` (object).
+- **Verified**: `const v = getHistory("doc1")[0]; typeof v.id === "string"; typeof v.timestamp === "number"; typeof v.content === "object"`.
+
+### 2.6 Version IDs are unique
+- **Behavior**: No two versions have the same ID.
+- **Verified**: Create and update multiple documents. Collect all version IDs — no duplicates.
+
+### 2.7 getVersion returns specific version content
+- **Behavior**: `getVersion(id, versionId)` returns the content at that version (deep cloned).
+- **Verified**: `create("doc1", {a:1}); const h = getHistory("doc1"); getVersion("doc1", h[0].id)` returns `{a:1}`.
+
+### 2.8 getVersion returns deep clone
+- **Behavior**: `getVersion` returns a deep clone.
+- **Verified**: `const v = getVersion("doc1", vid); v.a = 99; getVersion("doc1", vid).a` is still `1`.
+
+### 2.9 getVersion throws for bad version ID
+- **Behavior**: `getVersion(id, badVersionId)` throws if version not found.
+- **Verified**: `create("doc1", {a:1}); getVersion("doc1", "nonexistent")` throws.
+
+### 2.10 getVersion throws for bad document ID
+- **Behavior**: `getVersion(badId, versionId)` throws if document not found.
+- **Verified**: `getVersion("nonexistent", "v1")` throws.
+
+### 2.11 History is branch-isolated (pre-merge)
+- **Behavior**: Version history on one branch only includes versions created on that branch.
+- **Verified**: Create doc on main (v1), branch to feature, update doc (v2), switch back to main — `getHistory("doc1")` on main only shows [v1].
+
+## 3. Branching
+
+### 3.1 Default branch is "main"
+- **Behavior**: The initial branch is "main".
+- **Verified**: `getBranch()` returns `"main"`.
+
+### 3.2 createBranch from current branch
+- **Behavior**: `createBranch("feature")` creates a branch from current state.
+- **Verified**: On main, create doc1={a:1}. `createBranch("feature")`. `switchBranch("feature")`. `get("doc1")` returns `{a:1}`.
+
+### 3.3 createBranch from specified branch
+- **Behavior**: `createBranch("name", "fromBranch")` creates from the named branch.
+- **Verified**: On main, create doc1={a:1}. `createBranch("feature", "main")`. `switchBranch("feature"); get("doc1")` returns `{a:1}`.
+
+### 3.4 switchBranch changes active branch
+- **Behavior**: After `switchBranch`, CRUD applies to that branch.
+- **Verified**: `createBranch("feature"). switchBranch("feature"). create("doc1", {a:1}). switchBranch("main"). get("doc1")` throws (doc only exists on feature).
+
+### 3.5 Branch isolation — changes not visible across branches
+- **Behavior**: Updates on one branch don't affect other branches.
+- **Verified**: Create doc1={a:1} on main. Branch to feature. Update doc1={b:2} on feature. Switch to main. `get("doc1")` returns `{a:1}`.
+
+### 3.6 Branch isolation — deletes not visible
+- **Behavior**: Delete on one branch doesn't affect other branches.
+- **Verified**: Create doc1={a:1} on main. Branch to feature. Delete doc1 on feature. Switch to main. `get("doc1")` returns `{a:1}`.
+
+### 3.7 listBranches returns all branches
+- **Behavior**: `listBranches()` returns an array of all branch names.
+- **Verified**: Default → `["main"]`. After creating feature1, feature2 → contains "main", "feature1", "feature2".
+
+### 3.8 getBranch returns current branch name
+- **Behavior**: `getBranch()` returns the active branch name.
+- **Verified**: After `switchBranch("feature")`, `getBranch()` returns `"feature"`.
+
+### 3.9 switchBranch to nonexistent throws
+- **Behavior**: `switchBranch("nope")` throws if branch doesn't exist.
+- **Verified**: `switchBranch("nonexistent")` throws.
+
+### 3.10 createBranch over existing name throws
+- **Behavior**: `createBranch("main")` throws since "main" already exists.
+- **Verified**: `createBranch("main")` throws.
+
+## 4. Merging — Basic
+
+### 4.1 Merge with no changes is a no-op
+- **Behavior**: `merge(source)` with no changes on either branch returns `applied: true` with empty merged/conflicts.
+- **Verified**: Create doc1, branch to feature, merge feature into main. `applied: true`, `merged: {}`, `conflicts: []`.
+
+### 4.2 Merge picks up changes from source branch
+- **Behavior**: Changes on source branch are merged into current branch.
+- **Verified**: Create doc1={a:1} on main. Branch to feature. Update doc1={a:2} on feature. Switch to main. Merge feature into main. `get("doc1")` returns `{a:2}`.
+
+### 4.3 Merge with no conflicts auto-applies
+- **Behavior**: When no conflicts, `applied: true` and merged content is applied to current branch.
+- **Verified**: Same as 4.2 — after merge, current branch reflects merged content.
+
+### 4.4 Merge applies to current branch only
+- **Behavior**: Merge updates current branch, source branch is unchanged.
+- **Verified**: After merge in 4.2, switch to feature — doc1 still `{a:2}` (unchanged by merge).
+
+### 4.5 Merge adds new documents from source
+- **Behavior**: Documents created on source branch appear in target after merge.
+- **Verified**: Create doc1 on main. Branch to feature. Create doc2 on feature. Switch to main, merge feature. `get("doc2")` returns doc2 content.
+
+### 4.6 Merge propagates deletions
+- **Behavior**: Documents deleted on source branch are deleted in target after merge (if no conflict).
+- **Verified**: Create doc1 on main. Branch to feature. Delete doc1 on feature. Switch to main, merge feature. `get("doc1")` throws (not found).
+
+## 5. Merging — Three-Way Structural
+
+### 5.1 Only one side changed a field — take that change
+- **Behavior**: If only source changed a field, the merge takes source's value.
+- **Verified**: Main: doc1={a:1, b:2}. Feature: doc1={a:1, b:99}. Merge feature into main. Result: {a:1, b:99}. No conflict.
+
+### 5.2 Both sides changed same field to same value — no conflict
+- **Behavior**: If both changed a field identically, merge uses that value, no conflict.
+- **Verified**: Main: doc1={a:1}. Feature: doc1={a:1}. On main, update doc1={a:99}. On feature, update doc1={a:99}. Merge feature into main. `get("doc1")` returns `{a:99}`. Conflicts is empty.
+
+### 5.3 Both sides changed same field to different values — conflict
+- **Behavior**: Conflicting changes are reported.
+- **Verified**: Main: doc1={a:1}. Feature: doc1={a:1}. On main, update doc1={a:2}. On feature, update doc1={a:3}. Merge feature into main. `applied: false`. Conflicts has one entry: `{documentId: "doc1", path: "a", base: 1, ours: 2, theirs: 3}`.
+
+### 5.4 Merge conflict not applied to current branch
+- **Behavior**: When there are conflicts, `applied: false` and branch state is unchanged.
+- **Verified**: After merge with conflict (5.3), `get("doc1")` on main still returns `{a:2}` (unchanged).
+
+### 5.5 Merged field always contains merge result (ours-wins for conflicts)
+- **Behavior**: `merged` field in MergeResult contains the result with conflicts resolved in favor of ours.
+- **Verified**: After 5.3 conflict, `merged["doc1"]` is `{a:2}` (ours value).
+
+### 5.6 Nested object merge
+- **Behavior**: Three-way merge works on nested objects at field level.
+- **Verified**: Base: `{x: {y: 1, z: 2}}`. Ours: `{x: {y: 1, z: 99}}`. Theirs: `{x: {y: 2, z: 2}}`. Merge: both changed different nested fields → no conflict, merged = `{x: {y: 2, z: 99}}`.
+
+### 5.7 Conflicting nested path reported correctly
+- **Behavior**: Conflict path uses dot-separated notation for nested fields.
+- **Verified**: Base: `{a: {b: {c: 1}}}`. Ours: `{a: {b: {c: 2}}}`. Theirs: `{a: {b: {c: 3}}}`. Conflict: `path: "a.b.c"`.
+
+## 6. Merging — Multiple Documents
+
+### 6.1 Different documents on different branches merge cleanly
+- **Behavior**: Changes to different documents on different branches produce no conflicts.
+- **Verified**: Main has doc1={a:1}, doc2={b:2}. Branch to feature. Main updates doc1={a:99}. Feature updates doc2={b:99}. Merge feature into main. No conflicts. doc1={a:99}, doc2={b:99}.
+
+### 6.2 Complex multi-document, multi-branch merge
+- **Behavior**: Mix of created, updated, and unchanged documents across branches.
+- **Verified**: Main: doc1={a:1}, doc2={b:2}. Branch A updates doc1. Branch B updates doc2. Merge B into A → no conflicts, both changes applied.
+
+## 7. Edge Cases
+
+### 7.1 Merge with empty source branch
+- **Behavior**: Merging a branch that has no documents is valid.
+- **Verified**: Create doc1 on main. Branch to empty-feature (no changes). Merge empty-feature into main. No-op, doc1 unchanged.
+
+### 7.2 Array fields are compared as values
+- **Behavior**: Array fields are compared as whole values (not recursed into for merge).
+- **Verified**: Base: `{arr: [1,2]}`. Ours: `{arr: [1,2,3]}`. Theirs: `{arr: [1,2]}`. Only theirs unchanged → take ours. Or if both changed to different arrays → conflict at path "arr".
+
+### 7.3 Null field values
+- **Behavior**: Fields with null values are handled correctly.
+- **Verified**: Base: `{a: null}`. Ours: `{a: 1}`. Theirs: `{a: null}`. Only ours changed → no conflict, result: `{a: 1}`.
+
+### 7.4 Deep clone prevents cross-branch mutation
+- **Behavior**: Getting a document on one branch and mutating it doesn't affect another branch's copy.
+- **Verified**: Create doc with nested object on main. Branch to feature. Get doc on main and mutate. Get doc on feature — unchanged.
+
+## 8. Merge edge cases
+
+### 8.1 merge(source) where source == current branch
+- **Behavior**: Merging current branch into itself returns no-op.
+- **Verified**: `merge(getBranch())` returns `{applied: true, merged: {}, conflicts: []}`.
+
+### 8.2 Branching from a non-main branch
+- **Behavior**: Branching from feature to subfeature, then merging back.
+- **Verified**: Main doc1={a:1}. Feature doc1={a:2}. Subfeature (from feature) doc1={a:3}. Merge subfeature into feature — works correctly, LCA is feature's state.
+
+### 8.3 Merge with fromBranch parameter
+- **Behavior**: `createBranch("name", "fromBranch")` works across the full lifecycle.
+- **Verified**: Create doc1 on main. Create branch B from main. Create doc2 on B. Switch to main and merge B. doc2 exists on main after merge.
+
+## 9. Error handling for merge
+
+### 9.1 merge nonexistent branch throws
+- **Behavior**: `merge("nonexistent")` throws.
+- **Verified**: `merge("no-such-branch")` throws.
+
+### 9.2 Timestamps are set on versions
+- **Behavior**: Each version has a non-zero timestamp.
+- **Verified**: All versions have `timestamp > 0`.
+
+### 9.3 Concurrent version isolation
+- **Behavior**: Different documents have independent version counters.
+- **Verified**: Creating doc1 and doc2 produces unique version IDs across documents.
+
+## 10. Merge with changes on both branches, different fields
+
+### 10.1 Both branches modify different fields — no conflict
+- **Behavior**: Different fields changed on each branch merge cleanly.
+- **Verified**: Base: `{a:1, b:2}`. Ours: `{a:99, b:2}`. Theirs: `{a:1, b:99}`. Result: `{a:99, b:99}`. No conflicts.
+
+### 10.2 Adding new fields on both branches — same field → conflict
+- **Behavior**: Both branches add the same new field with different values.
+- **Verified**: Base: `{a:1}`. Ours: `{a:1, b:2}`. Theirs: `{a:1, b:3}`. Conflict at path "b".
+
+### 10.3 Adding new fields on both branches — different fields → no conflict
+- **Behavior**: Both branches add different new fields.
+- **Verified**: Base: `{a:1}`. Ours: `{a:1, b:2}`. Theirs: `{a:1, c:3}`. Result: `{a:1, b:2, c:3}`. No conflicts.
